&lt;li&gt;Advanced knowledge of Jamf products and solutions (Required)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced knowledge of IT ecosystem and key partner integrations/complementary solutions including but not limited to Apple, Okta, Microsoft, CrowdStrike, Zscaler, SIEM/SOAR (Preferred)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Specialized expertise in minimum 2 of the following areas: endpoint security architectures, identity and access management, zero-trust network architectures, SIEM/SOAR integration, API development and automation frameworks, Infrastructure as Code, emerging technologies (AI/ML, Apple Intelligence) (Preferred)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with scripting and automation languages (Go, Python, PowerShell, bash, Terraform, Ansible) and Apple developer languages (Swift, SwiftUI, Objective-C, Apple SDKs, Xcode) (Preferred)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience responding to RFPs and developing comprehensive solution proposals (Required)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to translate complex technical concepts into business outcomes for executives and decision-makers (Required)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong workshop and facilitation skills to align technical and business stakeholders (Preferred)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and oral communication skills in English (Required)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable engaging with a wide range of personnel, from technical to executive positions (Required)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience identifying solution gaps, ability to propose innovations, and execute subsequent implementation strategies (Preferred)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active participation in the Apple enterprise community including conferences, forums, user groups, thought leadership content, or public speaking (Preferred)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
