&lt;p&gt;We know why you are reading about this opportunity. You are driven to achieve goals. You are looking to make a direct impact. You want to work in a culture where your co-workers work as part of a diverse team, communicate across departments, and have a positive attitude. If we had to guess, you are innovative with great ideas, want to bring efficiencies to processes, and are looking to grow your career. Are we right? If so, let’s talk more!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Global Studies Coordinator (based in France) is responsible for supporting the team of Global Study Managers in the planning and operations of active clinical trial studies. The Coordinator is the main point of contact for patient communications and the management of all patient travel and logistical details.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Please note: The internal title for this role is &#39;Global Study Coordinator.&#39; This is a contract position. It is part-time, potentially up to 25 hours per week, and pays on an hourly basis. Hours are not guaranteed.&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manages travel and transportation budget for trial participants&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participates in discussions with vendors and internal team members regarding trial participant requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supports hospital or clinical staff relating to trial participant enrollments and visit schedules&lt;/li&gt;
